        "original_id": "0a7c1a4f-e84e-50b8-aa59-0a1a8365c584",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Balston, Count Gianbattista Spaletti, Count Cesare Spaletti, William of Wykeham\n- Organizations: Duckworth and Co., New College, Oxford, Eton\n- Families: Whatman family\n- Places: Italy, Oxford\n- Topics: English book production, illustration\n\nFacts:\n- New College, Oxford, was founded in 1379 by William of Wykeham.\n- The full name of New College, Oxford, is The Warden and Scholars of St Mary's College of Winchester in Oxford.\n- Thomas Balston was born in 1883 and died in 1967.\n- Thomas Balston was a member of the Whatman paper-making family.\n- Thomas Balston was educated at Eton and at New College, Oxford.\n- Before Thomas Balston was called to the bar in 1909, he served in Italy as tutor to Count Gianbattista Spaletti and Count Cesare Spaletti.\n- Thomas Balston became a director of the publishers Duckworth and Co.\n- Thomas Balston was a noted scholar of English book production and illustration.",
